<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105917" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυνδάρεος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Tyndareos,</i>
			husband of Leda, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.298
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				24.199
			</span></i> (cf. Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				2.151
			</span></i>), and <i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i> in lyr. passages (<i><span class="en">
				<u>El.</u>
				117
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				989
			</span></i>) acc. to codd. (prob. f.l.); 
				Att.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυνδάρεως</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εω</span>, ὁ, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				83
			</span></i> (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.9
			</span></i>, title of tragedy by <i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i> (gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εω</span> also in <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				94.7
			</span></i>, but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Fr.</u>
					96.21
				</span></i>
			):—hence Patron. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυνδᾰρίδης</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ</span>], 
				Dor.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τύμωλ-δας</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				10.73
			</span></i>, etc.; pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ Τυνδαρίδαι,</span>
			of Castor and Pollux, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Hom.</u>
				17.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.145
			</span></i>, etc. —Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυνδάρειος</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				137
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IT</u>
				5
			</span></i>; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Or.</u>
				1512
			</span></i> (troch.), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				919
			</span></i>:—fem. Patron. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυνδᾰρίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>, ἡ
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, παῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					1546
				</span></i>
			, etc.</div>
